{"book":{"id":"book-emancipation-the-union-army-and-the-reelection-of-abraham-lincoln-jonathan-w-white","slug":"emancipation-the-union-army-and-the-reelection-of-abraham-lincoln-jonathan-w-white","title":"Emancipation, the Union Army, and the Reelection of Abraham Lincoln","authors":[{"id":"person-jonathan-w-white","name":"Jonathan W. White"}],"publisherId":"publisher-louisiana-state-university-press","imprintId":"imprint-lsu-press","isbn13":["9780807174326"],"subjects":["War & Military"],"topics":["American Civil War","Slavery & Emancipation","Democracy & Elections","Soldiers, Veterans & Combat Experience"],"centralFigures":[],"links":{"amazon":"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Emancipation%2C%20the%20Union%20Army%2C%20and%20the%20Reelection%20of%20Abraham%20Lincoln%20Jonathan%20W.%20White","bookshop":"https://bookshop.org/search?keywords=Emancipation%2C%20the%20Union%20Army%2C%20and%20the%20Reelection%20of%20Abraham%20Lincoln%20Jonathan%20W.%20White","indiebound":"https://www.indiebound.org/search/book?keys=Emancipation%2C%20the%20Union%20Army%2C%20and%20the%20Reelection%20of%20Abraham%20Lincoln%20Jonathan%20W.%20White","worldcat":"https://search.worldcat.org/search?q=Emancipation%2C%20the%20Union%20Army%2C%20and%20the%20Reelection%20of%20Abraham%20Lincoln%20Jonathan%20W.%20White","publisher":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL29890176M"},"sourceIds":["source-award-record-lincoln-prize-civil-war-era-gettysburg-college-previous-winners-of-the-gilder-lehrman-lincoln-pr","source-open-library-emancipation-the-union-army-and-the-reelection-of-abraham-lincoln-jonathan-w-white"],"publicationYear":2014,"pageCount":296,"summary":"The Union army's overwhelming vote for Abraham Lincoln's reelection in 1864 has led many Civil War scholars to conclude that the soldiers supported the Republican Party and its effort to abolish slavery. In Emancipation, the Union Army, and the Reelection of Abraham Lincoln Jonathan W. White challenges this reigning paradigm in Civil War historiography, arguing instead that the soldier vote in the presidential election of 1864 is not a reliable index of the army's ideological motivation or political sentiment. Although 78 percent of the soldiers' votes were cast for Lincoln, White contends that this was not wholly due to a political or social conversion to the Republican Party. Rather, he argues, historians have ignored mitigating factors such as voter turnout, intimidation at the polls, and how soldiers voted in nonpresidential elections in 1864.","thumbnailUrl":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9002539-L.jpg","displaySummary":"The Union army's overwhelming vote for Abraham Lincoln's reelection in 1864 has led many Civil War scholars to conclude that the soldiers supported the Republican Party and its effort to abolish slavery. In Emancipation, the Union Army, and the Reelection of Abraham Lincoln Jonathan W. White challenges this reigning paradigm in Civil War historiography, arguing instead that the soldier vote in the presidential election of 1864 is not a reliable index of the army's ideological motivation or political sentiment. Although 78 percent of the soldiers' votes were cast for Lincoln, White contends that this was not wholly due to a political or social conversion to the Republican Party. Rather, he argues, historians have ignored mitigating factors such as voter turnout, intimidation at the polls, and how soldiers voted in nonpresidential elections in 1864.","primarySubject":"War & Military","primaryTopic":"American Civil War","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"War & Military","confidence":"low","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"War & Military","score":7,"evidenceCount":4},{"subject":"American History","score":5,"evidenceCount":3},{"subject":"Politics & Government","score":3,"evidenceCount":2},{"subject":"Society & Culture","score":2,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"award_category","rawLabel":"Gilder Lehrman Lincoln Prize: Civil War Era","mappedSubject":"American Histo